WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:02.470
- Every once in a while
I'll eat canned food,

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.971
but it's usually like in
a dark time of my life.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.844
The Weirdest Canned Food Taste Test

00:00:09.844 --> 00:00:13.647
- [Voiceover] Brown
bread, raisin flavored!

00:00:13.647 --> 00:00:14.648
- You're gonna have to...

00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:17.217
- Oh.

00:00:17.222 --> 00:00:18.218
- Oh, it's coming.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.120
I loosened it for you.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.087
- Yeah, sure.

00:00:22.732 --> 00:00:24.024
- I like it.

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:27.194
- Oh, it's so "raisin-y".

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:29.096
- It doesn't taste like raisins, though.

00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:31.198
- I do feel, though, if
they would serve this to me

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:32.966
on a plate at a fancy restaurant,

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.302
I'd be like "oh, chante, this is amazeur".

00:00:35.302 --> 00:00:36.804
- You can can bread.

00:00:36.804 --> 00:00:39.172
- I, for one, would rather die by zombies.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.874
- [Voiceover] A sample of rattlesnake meat

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.042
in the purest form.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:45.345
- Aah, no! I don't even want
to eat normal rattlesnake,

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.880
let alone in a can.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.815
- God, it's awful looking.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.617
- How we go from bread to rattlesnakes?

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.718
How did that happen?

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.253
- (laughs) This was a
very quick escalation.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.756
- That smells pretty damn good.

00:00:55.756 --> 00:00:56.756
- Smell it, smell it, smell it.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.924
- No, that's from a snake.

00:00:59.808 --> 00:01:00.961
(man laughs)

00:01:00.961 --> 00:01:02.195
- [Both] Cheers.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:07.134
- Aah, I'm sorry, aah!

00:01:07.134 --> 00:01:09.402
- I mean, it's more like venison, pork...

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.106
- Ew, the spine, it's a spine!

00:01:12.106 --> 00:01:13.640
- There's a snake spine in here.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.243
- We work hard, we deserve
boneless canned food.

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:18.311
- And especially boneless rattlesnake.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.280
- Like, you could
definitely put this in foods

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.668
that a chicken would be in or something,

00:01:21.668 --> 00:01:23.096
(man laughs)

00:01:23.096 --> 00:01:24.284
and you could just pass
off and get away with it.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.585
- I hope there's a prize in here

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.287
and it's just a little rattle.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.923
- [Voiceover] It's octopus.
- [Man] It's octopus, oh!

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.424
- Ooh!

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.594
- [Both] Ugh!

00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:36.263
- Don't waste time nor
money in cooking it,

00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:38.575
cutting it, or keeping it frozen.

00:01:38.575 --> 00:01:39.773
- Oh, it's a tentacle!

00:01:39.773 --> 00:01:40.700
- Yeah, tentacle!

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.202
- When they get calamari,
all the white people are like

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.504
"oh, I want the rings,
I don't want this stuff

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.273
"with the tentacles".

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:48.041
- You would hang out with
people that say stuff like that.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.643
- Freshy fishy.

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:53.347
- It's too chewy, it's like it never ends.

00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:54.881
Like, I keep chewing it
to get it to go away.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:57.184
- I know, and then the
flavor keeps coming out.

00:01:57.184 --> 00:01:58.285
- I don't like it.

00:01:58.285 --> 00:01:59.987
- I mean, if you're trying to
improve your jaw strength--

00:01:59.987 --> 00:02:01.254
- [Woman] Yeah, like that.
- [Man] This is the best meal.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.689
- It feels like gum.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.293
- Ugh, stop it.

00:02:07.928 --> 00:02:10.564
- [Both men] Fried chicken in a can.

00:02:10.564 --> 00:02:12.166
- [Woman] Fried "chik'n".

00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:13.366
- So you're giving me
fried chicken in a can,

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.772
and it's not even real fried chicken?

00:02:14.772 --> 00:02:17.296
- Ooh, how does it, it does
not need to be that thick.

00:02:17.296 --> 00:02:18.544
(man laughs)

00:02:18.544 --> 00:02:20.707
- There's no reason it
needs to be this big.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.776
- It smells like dog
food, like one you mix in.

00:02:22.776 --> 00:02:24.845
- Oh yeah, it smells like Fancy Feast.

00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:26.446
- Hmm.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.652
- It became a liquid so fast.

00:02:31.652 --> 00:02:33.121
- We can call it fried
chicken, they're vegetarian,

00:02:33.121 --> 00:02:34.388
they won't know, they don't
know what fried chicken

00:02:34.388 --> 00:02:35.617
tastes like 'cause they're vegetarians.

00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:36.957
- It makes me feel lonely.

00:02:36.957 --> 00:02:38.625
- Are you gonna give us a fake turkey now?

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.492
- It's Thanksgiving, you're gonna give us

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.562
a fake processed turkey in a can?

00:02:41.562 --> 00:02:44.130
Jesus tap dancing Christ.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.267
- [Voiceover] Alligator
in Cajun-style gravy.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.892
- We got some Cajun-style "alligata"!

00:02:49.892 --> 00:02:50.570
(man laughs)

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.706
- That smells delightful.

00:02:52.706 --> 00:02:54.174
- It look primordial as shit.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.909
- Kind of smells like Cup O' Noodles

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.610
like with Sriracha in them.

00:02:58.164 --> 00:02:59.467
- Really Cajun.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:00.747
- Nice spice.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:02.916
- If I had to have a choice
during the Apocalypse

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.384
or whatever this would be it.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.686
- Like, too soft, it's too soft.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.255
- This opened up a whole new world for me

00:03:08.255 --> 00:03:09.790
'cause this is not bad.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.958
- I don't think most people
have alligator and rattlesnake

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.227
canned foods, but, for a
lot of people, canned food

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.829
is a reality, it's a part of life,

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:17.564
it's something you need eat to survive.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.702
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:18.702 --> 00:03:21.234
- The fact that I can sit here in a chair

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.837
surrounded by lights and say which ones I,

00:03:23.837 --> 00:03:26.072
joke about which ones
tasted disgusting to me,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.908
I mean, that's coming
from a place of privilege,

00:03:27.908 --> 00:03:30.343
and I don't forget for a
second how lucky we are.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.344
- Yeah.

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.147
- Also, fuck this and I don't
want to eat it ever again.

00:03:33.147 --> 00:03:33.623
- True.

00:03:33.623 --> 00:03:37.017
- How is smoke-flavor an ingredient?

00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:39.352
- I don't know, maybe they just
have a smoker standing there

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.553
at the end going (blows smoke).

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.621
- Ew.

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:45.859
- And now you "'ave" fried
chicken with smoke "flava".

00:03:47.165 --> 00:03:48.442
- So they're French as well?

00:03:48.442 --> 00:03:51.465
- I mean, if I had to hire a
person to smoke on my food,

00:03:51.465 --> 00:03:54.057
I would hire a French person,
'cause at least it'd be sexy.

